    "body": "Refreshes three documentation files to match main after PR #121 (ADR-014). No source code changes.\n\n## The problem\n\n`docs/current-state.md` and the README feature matrix were written before ADR-014. They currently tell a stranger:\n\n- \"UA stylesheet: not implemented, planned for ADR-014 (next)\"\n- \"`<h1>` renders at 16px, same as `<p>`\"\n\nBoth are now false. `<h1>` renders at 32px, `<p>` has paragraph gaps, `<body>` has 8px margin. A stranger reading the docs today would learn wrong things about the code.\n\n## What changed\n\n**`docs/current-state.md`**:\n- UA stylesheet moves from \"does not render\" to \"renders correctly\" with #121.\n- The example.com section gains one note: the paragraph now has ~16px margin above and below from UA `p { margin: 1em 0 }`. The author `body { margin: auto }` correctly overrides UA `body { margin: 8px }` -- that override is the origin-aware cascade working as designed.\n\n**`README.md`**: UA stylesheet row flips from `:x:` to `:white_check_mark:`.\n\n**`docs/decisions/README.md`**: adds ADR-014, reading order updated to \"008 through 014\".\n\n## Written from screenshots, not tests\n\nTwo screenshots were used as source of truth:\n\n1. Welcome page after ADR-014 (PR #121): shows `h1` visibly larger (~32px), paragraph gaps, ~8px body inset.\n2. Example.com after ADR-014: single line of text with ~16px margin above and below (UA `p { margin: 1em 0 }`), still left-aligned and uncentered because `text-align` and `max-width` are not implemented.\n\nEvery claim in the diff traces to one of those two screenshots. In particular: **example.com has no `<h1>`**, so no `h1` comparison is claimed. An earlier draft of this refresh would have falsely described an `h1` on example.com -- that was caught before commit.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Build: no-op (docs only)\n- Tests: 165 cases, 669 assertions, unchanged\n- All three files grep-verified after edit\n\n## What is still stale (deferred)\n\n`docs/demo-screenshot.png` is from before ADR-014. It still accurately shows the demo page (author CSS overrides UA at every property the demo sets), so it does not need refreshing.\n\n## Next\n\nADR-015: inline formatting. Biggest remaining structural gap. `<span>`, `<a>`, `<em>` currently render as blocks and text does not wrap. That is what turns v0.2.0 into a browser that renders paragraphs the way their authors wrote them.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-20T11:33:51Z",
